.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt EPOLL 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm epoll_create ,
.Nm epoll_create1 ,
.Nm epoll_ctl ,
.Nm epoll_wait ,
.Nm epoll_pwait ,
.Nm epoll_pwait2
.Nd I/O event notification for many file descriptors
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/epoll.h
.Ft int
.Fn epoll_create "int size"
.Ft int
.Fn epoll_create1 "int flags"
.Ft int
.Fn epoll_ctl "int epfd" "int op" "int fd" "struct epoll_event *event"
.Ft int
.Fn epoll_wait "int epfd" "struct epoll_event *events" "int maxevents" "int timeout"
.Ft int
.Fo epoll_pwait
.Fa "int epfd"
.Fa "struct epoll_event *events"
.Fa "int maxevents"
.Fa "int timeout"
.Fa "const sigset_t *sigmask"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo epoll_pwait2
.Fa "int epfd"
.Fa "struct epoll_event *events"
.Fa "int maxevents"
.Fa "const struct timespec *timeout"
.Fa "const sigset_t *sigmask"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An epoll instance watches a set of file descriptors and reports which of
them are ready for I/O.
It is a
.Xr kqueue 2
with the event model of the Linux epoll interface:
each registered descriptor gives at most one event for each wait, and the
reported events are the
.Xr poll 2
events of the descriptor.
.Pp
The
.Fn epoll_create1
function returns a new epoll instance.
The
.Fa flags
argument is 0 or
.Dv EPOLL_CLOEXEC ,
which sets the close-on-exec flag of the new descriptor.
The
.Fn epoll_create
function is the same as
.Fn epoll_create1
with no flags; its
.Fa size
argument must be greater than 0 and has no other effect.
.Pp
The
.Fn epoll_ctl
system call changes the registration of the descriptor
.Fa fd
in the instance
.Fa epfd .
The
.Fa op
argument is one of:
.Bl -tag -width EPOLL_CTL_ADD
.It Dv EPOLL_CTL_ADD
Register
.Fa fd
with the events and the data of
.Fa event .
.It Dv EPOLL_CTL_MOD
Replace the events and the data of the registration of
.Fa fd .
.It Dv EPOLL_CTL_DEL
Remove the registration of
.Fa fd .
A pending event of the registration is removed too.
The
.Fa event
argument can be
.Dv NULL .
.El
.Pp
The
.Vt epoll_event
structure is:
.Bd -literal
typedef union epoll_data {
	void		*ptr;
	int		fd;
	uint32_t	u32;
	uint64_t	u64;
} epoll_data_t;

struct epoll_event {
	uint32_t	events;	/* epoll events */
	epoll_data_t	data;	/* user data */
};
.Ed
.Pp
The kernel returns
.Va data
unchanged with each event of the registration.
The
.Va events
field is a combination of these flags:
.Bl -tag -width EPOLLEXCLUSIVE
.It Dv EPOLLIN
The descriptor is readable.
.It Dv EPOLLOUT
The descriptor is writable.
.It Dv EPOLLRDHUP
The peer of a socket shut down its writing side.
.It Dv EPOLLPRI
Out-of-band data is available.
.It Dv EPOLLRDNORM , EPOLLRDBAND , EPOLLWRNORM , EPOLLWRBAND
As the
.Xr poll 2
events of the same names.
.It Dv EPOLLERR
An error condition.
It is always reported and need not be requested.
.It Dv EPOLLHUP
The descriptor was hung up.
It is always reported and need not be requested.
.It Dv EPOLLET
Edge-triggered: report the registration once for each change of state of
the descriptor, not for as long as it stays ready.
.It Dv EPOLLONESHOT
Report the registration once, then disable it until the next
.Dv EPOLL_CTL_MOD .
.It Dv EPOLLEXCLUSIVE
Accepted with
.Dv EPOLL_CTL_ADD
only, with
.Dv EPOLLIN ,
.Dv EPOLLOUT ,
.Dv EPOLLWAKEUP ,
.Dv EPOLLET ,
.Dv EPOLLERR
and
.Dv EPOLLHUP .
All instances that watch the descriptor are woken.
.It Dv EPOLLWAKEUP
Accepted and ignored.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Dv EPOLLET
and
.Dv EPOLLONESHOT ,
a registration is level-triggered: each wait reports it while the descriptor
is ready.
.Pp
The
.Fn epoll_pwait2
system call waits for events of the instance
.Fa epfd
and stores at most
.Fa maxevents
of them in
.Fa events .
A
.Dv NULL
.Fa timeout
waits without a limit; a zero
.Fa timeout
does not wait.
If
.Fa sigmask
is not
.Dv NULL ,
it replaces the signal mask of the thread during the wait, as with
.Xr ppoll 2 .
The
.Fn epoll_pwait
and
.Fn epoll_wait
functions are the same with a
.Fa timeout
in milliseconds, where a negative value waits without a limit.
.Pp
A registration belongs to the descriptor number.
It ends when the descriptor is closed.
A child that
.Xr fork 2
creates gets a copy of the instance with copies of the registrations, except
the registrations of other epoll instances and kqueues.
An epoll instance can be registered in another epoll instance or in a
kqueue.
It is readable when one of its registrations may be ready.
.Pp
.Xr kevent 2
cannot be used on an epoll instance.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn epoll_create
and
.Fn epoll_create1
functions return a new file descriptor.
The
.Fn epoll_ctl
system call returns 0.
The
.Fn epoll_wait ,
.Fn epoll_pwait
and
.Fn epoll_pwait2
functions return the number of events stored, or 0 if the timeout expired.
On error, \-1 is returned and
.Va errno
is set to indicate the error.
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn epoll_create
and
.Fn epoll_create1
functions fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The
.Fa size
argument is not greater than 0, or
.Fa flags
has a flag other than
.Dv EPOLL_CLOEXEC .
.It Bq Er EMFILE
The process has reached its limit for open file descriptors.
.It Bq Er ENFILE
The system file table is full.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
The process has reached its limit of kqueues
.Pq Dv RLIMIT_KQUEUES .
.El
.Pp
The
.Fn epoll_ctl
system call fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa epfd
or
.Fa fd
is not a valid file descriptor.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
.Fa op
is
.Dv EPOLL_CTL_ADD
and
.Fa fd
is already registered.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa event
points outside the address space of the process.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa epfd
is not an epoll instance,
.Fa fd
is the same as
.Fa epfd ,
.Fa op
is not valid, or
.Dv EPOLLEXCLUSIVE
is used with
.Dv EPOLL_CTL_MOD ,
on a registration that was added with it, with another event, or with a
descriptor that is an epoll instance or a kqueue.
.It Bq Er ELOOP
.Fa fd
is an epoll instance or a kqueue, and the registration would make a loop
of instances or a chain of more than 5 instances.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
.Fa op
is
.Dv EPOLL_CTL_MOD
or
.Dv EPOLL_CTL_DEL
and
.Fa fd
is not registered.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
No memory was available for the registration.
.It Bq Er EPERM
.Fa fd
refers to a regular file, a directory, or another file that cannot be
watched.
.It Bq Er EPIPE
.Fa fd
is the write end of a pipe whose read end is closed, and the events ask for
writing.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fn epoll_wait ,
.Fn epoll_pwait
and
.Fn epoll_pwait2
functions fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa epfd
is not a valid file descriptor.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa events ,
.Fa timeout
or
.Fa sigmask
points outside the address space of the process.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal was delivered before an event or the end of the timeout.
The call is not restarted.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa epfd
is not an epoll instance,
.Fa maxevents
is not greater than 0 or is too large, or
.Fa timeout
is not a valid time.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kevent 2 ,
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr poll 2 ,
.Xr ppoll 2 ,
.Xr select 2
.Sh STANDARDS
These functions are non-standard.
They are present in Linux.
.Sh HISTORY
These functions first appeared in the freebsd-android-native fork of
.Fx 15.1 .
.Sh BUGS
A registration ends when its descriptor number is closed, even if another
descriptor of the same open file stays open.
An epoll instance is copied, not shared, by
.Xr fork 2 ,
and cannot be passed with
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS .
The functions are not cancellation points.
